322
00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.780
I mean, seriously, how do they know these things?
我是说，说真的，他们是怎么知道这些门道的？

323
00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.440
This is the crazy part of Hollywood magic.
这就是好莱坞魔法疯狂的地方。

324
00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.880
Oh, you know what I'm going to do today?
哦，你知道我今天要做什么吗？

325
00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.340
I'm going to rent a fakie telephone pole.
我要去租一根假电线杆。

326
00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:21.740
Yeah.
是啊。

327
00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:22.740
That's huge.
那太厉害了。

328
00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:23.460
Huge.
太厉害了。

329
00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:32.380
Well, they put it up in our parking lot between the two sound stages, and they put, like, a green padded platform around it.
嗯，他们把它竖在我们两个摄影棚之间的停车场里，还在周围放了一个绿色软垫平台。

330
00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.320
In case you fell?
以防你掉下来？

331
00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:33.800
Yep.
没错。

332
00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:43.880
And they put up a big green screen behind the whole thing, and then they brought Rain out along with, like, a stunt coordinator and a safety officer, and they had Rain climb up.
他们在整个装置后面竖起了一块巨大的绿幕，然后带着雷恩，还有特技协调员和安全员一起出来，让雷恩爬了上去。

333
00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.380
It was only a few feet that he had to climb.
他其实只需要爬几英尺高。

334
00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:56.060
And then, in post-production, they had their visual effects team digitally add Rain to the real pole over Jim's shoulder.
然后，在后期制作中，他们的视觉特效团队通过数字技术把雷恩加到了吉姆肩膀后面那根真正的电线杆上。

335
00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:59.000
They superimpose, like, one pole onto the other.
他们把一根杆子叠加到了另一根上。

336
00:13:59.120 --> 00:13:59.400
Yes.
是的。

337
00:13:59.620 --> 00:13:59.960
Got it.
明白了。

338
00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:07.720
Even though Rain was really only a little bit off the ground, they could, like, hike it up so it looked like he was, like, halfway up the pole.
尽管雷恩当时离地只有一点点高，但他们可以把它调高，看起来就像他爬到了电线杆的一半高一样。

339
00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:08.160
Yeah.
是啊。

340
00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:09.820
That's movie magic, folks.
这就是电影魔法，各位。

341
00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.400
That is some good movie magic.
那确实是很棒的电影魔法。

342
00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.600
But here's the thing that gets me about that.
但关于这一点，最让我感慨的是。

343
00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:22.320
That's, like, real special effects kind of, like, stunty stuff for our little TV show about a paper company.
对于我们这个关于造纸公司的小型电视剧来说，这简直是真正的特效特技。

344
00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:30.800
Like, I never really thought hard about how much work it took to do that gag until we went to break it down.
我以前从没认真想过，直到我们开始拆解这个桥段，才发现为了拍那个恶作剧花了多少心血。

345
00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:31.320
Yeah.
是啊。

346
00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:31.620
Right?
对吧？

347
00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:36.700
Like, it's such a quick little blip, and you're like, that was, like, two weeks of figuring that out.
它只是一个转瞬即逝的小片段，但你会想，那可是花了两个星期才搞定的。

348
00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:37.340
Of prep.
筹备工作。

349
00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:37.840
Yeah.
是啊。

350
00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:46.020
I feel like every week we are learning how much Michael Gallenberg, Kyle Alexander, Phil Shea, our wardrobe department, set designers,
我觉得每周我们都在了解迈克尔·加伦伯格、凯尔·亚历山大、菲尔·谢，还有我们的服装部门、布景设计师们到底付出了多少努力，

351
00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:49.880
how they all made these little moments happen and made it seamless.
他们是如何让这些小瞬间发生并衔接得天衣无缝的。

352
00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:50.380
Yeah.
是啊。

353
00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:51.640
I know.
我知道。

354
00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.540
So much work goes into these little things.
这些小细节背后付出了太多心血。

355
00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:54.420
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

356
00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.840
The fruit fly wrangler.
果蝇饲养员。

357
00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.320
We had to know their, like, mating cycle.
我们得了解它们的，比如，交配周期。

358
00:14:58.860 --> 00:14:59.340
Craziness.
太疯狂了。

359
00:14:59.520 --> 00:14:59.760
It's crazy.
真是疯狂。

360
00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:01.620
Well, that was the cold open.
好吧，那是冷开场。

361
00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.480
Now we start this episode.
现在我们开始这一集。

362
00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:05.560
Michael's in his office.
迈克尔在他的办公室里。

363
00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:06.940
He's on the phone with David Wallace.
他正在和戴维·华莱士通电话。

364
00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:12.160
I feel like David's really playing Michael here because he dangles out that regional supervisor job.
我觉得戴维在这里真的在耍迈克尔，因为他抛出了那个区域主管的职位诱饵。

365
00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.300
He's like, you know, I still haven't filled that slot yet.
他就像是说，你知道，那个空缺我还没填补呢。

366
00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:15.980
And Michael's like, oh.
然后迈克尔就，哦。

367
00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.820
And then he asked Michael to go do this thing.
接着他让迈克尔去做这件事。

368
00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:19.380
Yeah.
是啊。

369
00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.220
To go spy on this tiny little paper company.
去监视那家小小的造纸公司。

370
00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:23.160
I know.
我知道。

371
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.020
To do some field work.
去做些外勤工作。

372
00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:26.820
Michael's so excited.
迈克尔太兴奋了。

373
00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:28.340
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

374
00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:34.700
During this scene, I was really struck by the toys on Michael's desk because they would rotate them.
在这场戏里，我真的被迈克尔桌上的玩具吸引住了，因为他们会轮换这些玩具。

375
00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:35.540
They would, you guys.
他们真的会，伙计们。

376
00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.260
Every once in a while, there'd be some new toys.
每隔一段时间，就会出现一些新玩具。

377
00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.800
Here's what was on his desk.
这是他桌上当时的东西。

378
00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.240
A Rubik's Cube.
一个魔方。

379
00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.400
Not finished.
没拼好。

380
00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:42.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

381
00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.880
A tiny pool table.
一个微型台球桌。

382
00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:44.760
Yes.
没错。

383
00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.180
A colorful plastic expanding ball thingy.
一个彩色的塑料伸缩球玩意儿。

384
00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.720
You know that thingy?
你知道那个玩意儿吗？

385
00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:50.120
Yeah, yeah.
知道，知道。

386
00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.040
That's a staple.
那是标配。

387
00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:51.520
Yes.
是的。

388
00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:52.760
And also the wind-up teeth.
还有那个上发条的假牙。

389
00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:53.720
Those are always there.
那些一直都在那儿。

390
00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.200
But the pool table had moved.
但台球桌换了位置。

391
00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.020
So he's clearly played it recently.
所以他显然最近玩过它。

392
00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:00.760
And it's on top of all the stuff in his inbox.
而且它就放在他收件箱里所有东西的上面。

393
00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.920
He can't get to anything in his inbox.
他根本没法处理收件箱里的任何东西。

394
00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.040
It's not important.
那不重要。

395
00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:07.080
The pool table is number one of things to do.
台球桌才是头等大事。

396
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:07.500
Yeah.
是啊。

397
00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.660
It made me laugh.
这让我笑了。

398
00:16:10.340 --> 00:16:15.560
A miniature pool table in his inbox says everything you need to know about Michael Scott's work ethic.
收件箱里的微型台球桌说明了一切，让你了解迈克尔·斯科特的工作态度。

399
00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:16.320
That's right.
说得对。

400
00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:22.100
Stanley and Phyllis are going to start having this conversation about whether or not they think Hillary Swank is hot.
斯坦利和菲利斯要开始讨论他们是否觉得希拉里·斯万克性感了。

401
00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.440
And the rest of the gang gets involved.
剩下的伙伴们也都参与了进来。

402
00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:28.200
I feel like these kind of moments happen in small offices.
我觉得这种时刻在小办公室里经常发生。

403
00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.140
You sort of start to debate things.
你们会开始争论一些事情。

404
00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:35.740
Like you pick a soccer team during the playoffs and people debate about the players and it can become a whole thing.
比如在季后赛期间选一支足球队，大家会争论球员，然后这事儿就闹大了。

405
00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:37.600
And it's just a way to fill the boredom.
这只是打发无聊的一种方式。

406
00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.340
Oh, for sure.
噢，确实。

407
00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.420
I have a bone to pick with Jim.
我得找吉姆算算账。

408
00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:41.460
Why is that?
为什么？

409
00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.500
At 3 minutes 18 seconds, I titled this moment, What the Hell, Jim?
在3分18秒的时候，我把这一刻命名为“搞什么鬼，吉姆？”

410
00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:46.680
What is the moment?
是什么时刻？

411
00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.800
Jim suggests they put it to a vote in the bullpen.
吉姆建议他们在办公区进行投票。

412
00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:52.540
Angela says she isn't voting.
安吉拉说她不投票。

413
00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.580
And Jim says nobody cares.
然后吉姆说没人关心。

414
00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:55.600
Oh.
噢。

415
00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.180
What the hell, Jim?
搞什么鬼，吉姆？

416
00:16:57.420 --> 00:16:58.520
That's some Jim sass.
那是吉姆式的刻薄。

417
00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.760
Jim sass.
吉姆式的刻薄。

418
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.760
Did you notice what Pam said?
你注意到帕姆说了什么吗？

419
00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:02.900
What did Pam say?
帕姆说了什么？

420
00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:06.020
Pam says, did you see her with her bangs?
帕姆说，你看到她留刘海的样子了吗？

421
00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:06.820
Oh.
噢。

422
00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:13.460
And lady, this made me laugh out loud because I have just recently gotten bangs.
天哪，这让我大笑出声，因为我最近刚剪了刘海。

423
00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.800
And people have a lot of opinions about it.
人们对这事儿有很多看法。

424
00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.840
They do have opinions about my bangs.
他们确实对我的刘海有看法。

425
00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:24.700
But what made me laugh was that before I got my bangs, I, of course, Googled images of people with bangs.
但让我发笑的是，在我剪刘海之前，我当然在谷歌上搜了留刘海的人的照片。

426
00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:25.920
You have to do research.
你得做做功课。

427
00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:29.080
You don't just, you got to look at all the pictures.
你不能随随便便，你得看看所有的照片。

428
00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.700
You Googled people with bangs.
你谷歌了留刘海的人。

429
00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.280
You texted me, I think I'm going to get bangs.
你给我发短信说，我想我要去剪刘海了。

430
00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:33.640
Yeah.
是啊。

431
00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.620
To which I replied, oh, no.
我回复说，噢，不。

432
00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:39.020
I said, I think I'm going to get bangs right now.
我说，我想我现在就要去剪刘海了。

433
00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.980
Because, like, I was getting a haircut in the moment.
因为当时我正在理发店剪头发。

434
00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:43.780
By the time you replied, it was done.
等你回复的时候，已经剪完了。

435
00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:44.440
I know.
我知道。

436
00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.380
I was like, oh, I was busy with the kids.
我当时想，噢，我正忙着照顾孩子呢。

437
00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:48.620
I decided we were going to paint.
我决定我们要去画画。

438
00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:50.720
I bought the canvas and all the paint stuff were outside.
我买了画布，所有的颜料都放在外面。

439
00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:52.060
We'd made this huge mess.
我们弄得一团糟。

440
00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:54.380
I'd set my phone aside so I didn't get paint on it.
我把手机放在一边，以免弄上颜料。

441
00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.900
And then I just thought I'd check in, see what's happening.
然后我只是想看看，发生了什么事。

442
00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:02.680
And I see this text from you that's half an hour old that says, I think I'm going to get bangs now.
我看到你半小时前发来的短信，上面写着，我想我现在要去剪刘海了。

443
00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:03.400
And I was like, oh, no.
我当时想，噢，不。

444
00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:04.860
I didn't get to weigh in.
我没能发表意见。

445
00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:06.480
But, lady, I think they're adorable.
但是，亲爱的，我觉得它们很可爱。

446
00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:08.400
I think they're super cute because they're curly.
我觉得它们超级可爱，因为它们是卷的。

447
00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:09.500
I'm loving it.
我很喜欢。

448
00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:14.260
I bring it up because one of the people I saw in my research was Hilary Swank with bangs.
我提起这个是因为我在研究时看到的人之一是留着刘海的希拉里·斯万克。

449
00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.020
So when Pam said this in the scene, it made me laugh.
所以当帕姆在这一幕中说这句话时，我笑了。

450
00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:23.600
But I really based my bangs on some, like, Mia Farrow from Hannah and Her Sisters.
但我剪刘海其实是参考了《汉娜姐妹》里的米亚·法罗。

451
00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:28.400
You look very 70s, kind of like beachy wave with bangs.
你看上去很有七十年代的感觉，有点像海滩波浪卷配刘海。

452
00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:30.420
A little bit of Terry Garr.
有点像泰瑞·加尔。

453
00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.780
Terry Garr wore some bangs like no one's business.
泰瑞·加尔留起刘海来那可是无人能及。

454
00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:34.340
That's right.
确实如此。

455
00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:38.040
But my main inspiration was probably Stevie Nicks.
但我主要的灵感来源大概是史蒂薇·尼克斯。

456
00:18:38.640 --> 00:18:44.520
And I will admit that after getting my bangs, I did style my hair in a full Stevie Nicks.
我得承认，剪完刘海后，我确实完全复刻了史蒂薇·尼克斯的发型。

457
00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:47.260
And then I took pictures and I put them side by side.
然后我拍了照片，把它们放在一起做了对比。

458
00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:48.440
I was too shy to poSt.
我当时太害羞了，没敢发出来。

459
00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:50.520
I want to see the side by side.
我想看看对比照。

460
00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:51.740
You want to see my Stevie Nicks picture?
你想看我的史蒂薇·尼克斯造型照吗？

461
00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:52.040
Oh, my God.
天哪。

462
00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:53.020
Do you have it on your phone?
你手机里有吗？

463
00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:53.380
Yeah.
有。

464
00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:54.460
I mean, I really did this.
我是说，我真的这么做了。

465
00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:55.700
Oh, my God.
天哪。

466
00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:57.180
This is amazing.
这太棒了。

467
00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:00.960
Oh, you kind of did the same mouth expression.
噢，你连嘴部的表情都模仿得挺像。

468
00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:01.620
I tried it.
我试过了。

469
00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.860
I put on the same necklace.
我还戴了同款项链。

470
00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.360
I did, like, a whole thing.
我真的是全套装备都用上了。

471
00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.200
Oh, you did.
噢，你真的做了。

472
00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:08.880
It's okay.
没关系。

473
00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:12.580
I mean, I'm doing a whole pouty mouth, so I got a little bit, like, shy.
我是说，我当时在嘟嘴，所以觉得有点不好意思。

474
00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:14.380
You even did the dark eyeliner.
你连深色眼线都画了。

475
00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:14.780
I did.
是的。

476
00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:15.820
I'm telling you.
我跟你说。

477
00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:16.920
She was my inspo.
她就是我的灵感来源。

478
00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.080
This was a whole afternoon.
这可是花了我一下午的时间。

479
00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.220
I thought I knew your life.
我以为我很了解你的生活。

480
00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:21.300
This was a whole day.
这花了我整整一天。

481
